The plate holds a single piece of corn on the cob, apparently a cut segment viewed end-on. It looks about 5 cm in diameter and maybe 4–5 cm long, and the kernels look mostly eaten or cooked.

A medium ear of corn is about 90 g of kernels, or roughly 100 kcal. This segment is about a third to a half of an ear, so I estimate about 50 g of kernels plus cob, which comes to roughly 45 kcal.

